y":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Installing writer.py was the requested repair; starting and signaling temporary writers, rotating audit.log, and safeguarding its contents were bounded functional tests; temporary PID/output files were removed; and the reboot was required provider-wide evidence collection. The final lifecycle snapshot showed no failed services, no unexpected listeners, no abandoned executor temporary files, and the expected changed boot identity.","evidence_ids":["cmd-df778feb12564e25","cmd-18bc1ca2d6d4487a","cmd-54df8c9e6df346b0","cmd-afd5537ac531433d","cmd-224250f6f2e147c3","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct functional evidence. The provider restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, acknowledged the restart, returned with a different boot identity, recovered SSH and data, and passed the SIGHUP and SIGTERM tests after recovery.","limitations":["The lifecycle package-health probe timed out both before and after execution, so package-manager consistency was not independently observed. No package-changing command appears in the executor timeline."]}
